Many believe that freedom means “doing what you want.”
But according to Jesus, true freedom is the ability to live in the light, outside of lies, outside of the slavery of sin, fear, doubt, ignorance.

When you remain in his Word:
    • You see life as God sees it;
    • You understand who you really are;
    • You are liberated internally.

5. A living Word, not just written

The Word of God is not just a text.
It is a living voice, a spirit, a divine force.

It has three dimensions:
    1. Written (logos) – What you read in the Bible;
    2. Revealed (rhema) – What God shows you in a specific moment;
    3. Living (Christ) – Jesus himself, the Word incarnate.

6. The role of the Holy Spirit

The Bible is not an intellectual manual:

Without the Holy Spirit, you can read without ever hearing God.

It is the Spirit who:
    • Gives understanding;
    • Open the eyes of the heart;
    • Transform what you read into living truth.

7. Why you need to be taught

God uses anointed men and women (teachers, pastors, prophets, etc.) to:
    • Help you better understand the Word;
    • Avoid mistakes and confusion;
    • Bring you higher in the knowledge of God.

But above all, it is the Spirit who confirms everything in your heart.

